[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3708007597","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114522#issuecomment-3708007597","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114522","id":3708007597,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dA7St","user":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-04T11:39:12Z","updated_at":"2026-01-04T11:39:12Z","body":"IMO this description is not imprecise, let's take the full phrase from docs:\n\n> Returns the minimum of the given numeric values. This function can take any number of arguments.\n\nThe first part make its clear the function will do a comparasion and for do a comparation you automaticly need two or more \"objects\" as you need the thing you want to compare and another thing to use as base/ruler. \n\nAlso, the function per se doesn't make sense be called with zero or one argument as you can't get the minimum of nothing and if you have only one \"object\" this will be automactly your minimum/maximum.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reacti